0026:     - Each frame's bounding-box border is either complete or has exactly one missing non-corner border pixel.
0027:     - Frame interiors and the outward line from each border gap are black in the input.
0028:     Rule
0029:     - For every frame, recolor all pixels strictly inside its bbox to teal.
0030:     - If the frame has a missing border pixel, recolor that gap and every black pixel from it straight outward, perpendicular to that side, through the grid edge.
0031:     - Keep the blue frame pixels and all other black background pixels unchanged.
0032:     Key insight
0033:     - A missing border pixel is not a defect to repair with blue; it is a doorway that defines the direction of the teal spill from the filled rectangle.
